# =============================================================================
# ops/tool-versions.env
#
# The tools installed around the application on every machine that builds,
# tests or runs it (workstations, continuous integration, the container images
# and the deployed hosts), each pinned to one exact version and, where it is
# fetched from outside an operating system's own signed repositories, to one
# checksum. Read by the workstation setup, the host bootstrap and the CloudWatch
# agent installers on the operator workstation; values bound for a host travel
# over the install pipe, and the host never reads this file.
#
# Kept here, beside the systemd units, because this directory holds what is
# installed around the application rather than what the application or one
# environment carries, and a pin written inside a script is a pin nobody finds
# when it needs to move. .nvmrc and .python-version stay at the repository root,
# where the Node and Python tooling reads them by name; the setup script
# cross-checks them against the pins here.
#
# One KEY=value per line, no quotes, no shell: the readers parse it with grep
# rather than sourcing it, so nothing here ever runs as code.
#
# A value beginning REPLACE_WITH_ is a placeholder. Every installer refuses to
# install while one is present, naming the key, because a checksum nobody has
# read is not a check. To fill a placeholder, download the artifact once on a
# trusted machine, compare its digest with the one the publisher lists, and
# write the digest here:
#
#   Compose plugin (the publisher lists its digest in the .sha256 file beside
#   the binary on the release page):
#     V=v5.1.0
#     U=https://github.com/docker/compose/releases/download/$V
#     curl -fsSL "$U/docker-compose-linux-x86_64" | sha256sum
#     curl -fsSL "$U/docker-compose-linux-x86_64.sha256"
#
#   CloudWatch agent (the current version is in info/latest/CWAGENT_VERSION in
#   the same bucket; the publisher signs the package rather than listing a
#   digest, so verify the signature with its key, whose fingerprint AWS
#   documents as 9376 16F3 450B 7D80 6CBD 9725 D581 6730 3B78 9C72, then pin
#   the digest of the verified package):
#     V=<version>
#     B=https://amazoncloudwatch-agent.s3.amazonaws.com
#     curl -fsSLO "$B/amazon_linux/amd64/$V/amazon-cloudwatch-agent.rpm"
#     curl -fsSLO "$B/amazon_linux/amd64/$V/amazon-cloudwatch-agent.rpm.sig"
#     curl -fsSLO "$B/assets/amazon-cloudwatch-agent.gpg"
#     gpg --import amazon-cloudwatch-agent.gpg
#     gpg --fingerprint 3B789C72
#     gpg --verify amazon-cloudwatch-agent.rpm.sig amazon-cloudwatch-agent.rpm
#     sha256sum amazon-cloudwatch-agent.rpm
#
# Moving a pin is a version and a digest changed together, in one commit.
# =============================================================================

# ── Hosts ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The Amazon Linux 2023 release the hosts are held to. The distribution locks a
# host to the repository version it was built from, so this release fixes the
# exact version of every package below that comes from its repositories; the
# versions named for those packages are what this release serves.
AMAZON_LINUX_RELEASE=2023.12.20261021

# The container engine, from Amazon Linux 2023's own repository. That package
# is signed by the distribution and verified by dnf, so it is named here rather
# than checksummed, and the distribution patches it. Docker's static builds are
# not used: Docker does not recommend them in production and they receive no
# automatic security updates. The Docker CE repository is not used either: it
# keys its paths on a RHEL release this distribution does not report, and
# returns nothing.
DOCKER_PACKAGE=docker
DOCKER_ENGINE_HOST=25.0.16-1.amzn2023.0.5

# The Compose plugin is not in the distribution's repositories, so it is the
# one binary fetched from its publisher, and the one that must match a digest
# before it is installed.
COMPOSE_VERSION=v5.1.0
COMPOSE_URL=https://github.com/docker/compose/releases/download/v5.1.0/docker-compose-linux-x86_64
COMPOSE_SHA256=5633cb21e06a7c88c7ca48a9334d3d0f7f892e9605ae9e9a45f9a095d4ffceb8

# The sqlite3 command-line tool: one version everywhere, equal to the engine
# better-sqlite3 bundles into the app (its deps/download.sh), so the backup, the
# restore and the deploy read and write files with the engine that wrote them.
# The backup's VACUUM INTO needs 3.27 or newer. Built by scripts/build-sqlite3.sh
# from sqlite.org's amalgamation as one static binary, because the prebuilt
# Linux tools need a newer C library than Amazon Linux 2023 and Ubuntu 22.04
# carry. Two digests: the zip's was computed when the pin was set, and the
# sqlite3.c inside it must also match the one sqlite.org publishes for the
# release, which ties the download to the publisher. The build runs in the
# image container's pinned base, with its compiler held to these versions. On a
# host the binary is built on the workstation and shipped over the install pipe,
# replacing the distribution's sqlite package, so no compiler reaches a host.
SQLITE_VERSION=3.51.2
SQLITE_SOURCE_URL=https://sqlite.org/2026/sqlite-amalgamation-3510200.zip
SQLITE_SOURCE_SHA3_256=9a9dd4eef7a97809bfacd84a7db5080a5c0eff7aaf1fc1aca20a6dc9a0c26f96
SQLITE_AMALGAMATION_SHA3_256=733b3fcc6cccb1e334424b9b91a9d68b618385b76ebfcbb106690bd3a9e61367
SQLITE_BUILD_GCC=gcc=15.2.0-r5
SQLITE_BUILD_MUSL_DEV=musl-dev=1.2.6-r3

# Plain distribution packages the deploy calls, at the version the pinned
# Amazon Linux release serves.
RSYNC_PACKAGE=rsync
# Installed only when the image ships no aws command of its own.
AWSCLI_PACKAGE=awscli-2

# The CloudWatch agent package, fetched from its publisher's bucket. The
# version is the path segment the publisher files the package under, which is
# also the version the agent reports about itself once running.
CWAGENT_VERSION=1.300074.0b1920
CWAGENT_URL=https://amazoncloudwatch-agent.s3.amazonaws.com/amazon_linux/amd64/1.300074.0b1920/amazon-cloudwatch-agent.rpm
CWAGENT_SHA256=41609c43d73747c7cf23f28c4ddfdc2370b80cd556aecd296190fc9cdb8c72a4

# ── Workstations ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The Docker CE engine a workstation runs, from Docker's Ubuntu repository,
# installed with an apt version pin. A different line from the hosts' engine:
# Docker's repository ended the 25.0 series long before the distribution's
# patched build, so the two cannot be the same version. The images, the
# Compose plugin and the compose files are what must match, and do.
DOCKER_ENGINE_WORKSTATION=5:29.3.0-1~ubuntu.22.04~jammy

# The standalone CPython build the setup script installs; its version must equal
# .python-version.
PYTHON_VERSION=3.12.12
PYTHON_URL=https://github.com/astral-sh/python-build-standalone/releases/download/20260211/cpython-3.12.12+20260211-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu-install_only.tar.gz
PYTHON_SHA256=4a867ae3436e9d7c3558a8fd2bd82e13dd0de59282e2f4e20e5c879f9085fe86

NVM_VERSION=0.40.3
NVM_URL=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nvm-sh/nvm/v0.40.3/install.sh
NVM_SHA256=2d8359a64a3cb07c02389ad88ceecd43f2fa469c06104f92f98df5b6f315275f

GITLEAKS_VERSION=8.24.3
GITLEAKS_URL=https://github.com/gitleaks/gitleaks/releases/download/v8.24.3/gitleaks_8.24.3_linux_x64.tar.gz
GITLEAKS_SHA256=9991e0b2903da4c8f6122b5c3186448b927a5da4deef1fe45271c3793f4ee29c

TERRAFORM_VERSION=1.14.7
TERRAFORM_URL=https://releases.hashicorp.com/terraform/1.14.7/terraform_1.14.7_linux_amd64.zip
TERRAFORM_SHA256=e8bbcefea8015156e04e2a325cde37a0b2fb761728bda548e2fe3b8ad7c18c96

# AWS publishes no checksum list for the CLI; this one was computed from the
# versioned installer when the pin was set, so it holds the download to that
# exact file like every other pin here.
AWS_CLI_VERSION=2.34.8
AWS_CLI_URL=https://awscli.amazonaws.com/awscli-exe-linux-x86_64-2.34.8.zip
AWS_CLI_SHA256=de4a8f35c5d19e120e6b5403bbebbf356459ae17af78941ae74e37a78f44aef3

# jq: the publisher lists this digest in the release's sha256sum.txt.
JQ_VERSION=1.7.1
JQ_URL=https://github.com/jqlang/jq/releases/download/jq-1.7.1/jq-linux-amd64
JQ_SHA256=5942c9b0934e510ee61eb3e30273f1b3fe2590df93933a93d7c58b81d19c8ff5

# age: the publisher lists no digest for this release; this one was computed
# from the release tarball when the pin was set.
AGE_VERSION=1.1.1
AGE_URL=https://github.com/FiloSottile/age/releases/download/v1.1.1/age-v1.1.1-linux-amd64.tar.gz
AGE_SHA256=cf16cbb108fc56e2064b00ba2b65d9fb1b8d7002ca5e38260ee1cc34f6aaa8f9

# ── Container images ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The image container's ffmpeg, from the Alpine release the pinned Node base
# image carries (Alpine 3.24).
FFMPEG_VERSION=8.1.3-r0

# Trivy, the advisory scanner scripts/check-versions.sh --advisories runs on
# request, never on a schedule: the maintainer decides when to patch. Pinned by
# the multi-architecture index digest Docker Hub lists for the release.
TRIVY_VERSION=0.76.1
TRIVY_IMAGE=aquasec/trivy:0.76.1@sha256:790fd66d1697395d8693d1acaa1ea702406a20f109b6fc7bac8db623eca6c06c

# The Amazon Linux 2023 container image at the hosts' pinned release, which the
# advisory scan reads as a stand-in for the hosts' operating-system packages.
# Moves with AMAZON_LINUX_RELEASE; pinned by the index digest Docker Hub lists for
# the release's tag.
AMAZONLINUX_IMAGE=amazonlinux:2023.12.20261021.0@sha256:c04a1012acc483977f61f7f91c28624a39a621e56a59781319a75dec528be9b6

# ── Application settings pinned beside the tools ─────────────────────────────

# The argon2 cost the application hashes every password with. Pinned here so a
# library upgrade cannot change it silently; src/lib/passwordHash.ts passes
# these values explicitly and a test holds the two together. Changing one means
# raising the password hash version, so older hashes are re-derived at sign-in.
ARGON2_TYPE=argon2id
ARGON2_MEMORY_KIB=65536
ARGON2_TIME_COST=3
ARGON2_PARALLELISM=4
ARGON2_HASH_LENGTH=32
